                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "475ff3cc-6cbb-3c48-8aef-8f949e425cbf",
                        "entry_id": "0c6c54a2-6175-3377-a031-a225f659fbe4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having blemishes; flawed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b016e97f-d5a4-4a79-9738-f751ee13ac2e",
                                "sense_id": "475ff3cc-6cbb-3c48-8aef-8f949e425cbf",
                                "text": "Stated sharply, today′s centers of higher learning are more blemished than superficial appearances suggest, and what often seems “democratic” is little more than contrived public displays."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3b43d99-a3d7-4a65-b58b-8a04047a1997",
                                "sense_id": "475ff3cc-6cbb-3c48-8aef-8f949e425cbf",
                                "text": "One of them in fact singled out Rebecca, not the marmoreal Rowena, as the novel′s most blemished character. “She is,” he complained, “too near perfection.[…]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4959ee31-bc2b-4cb6-8578-fab780295eb4",
                                "sense_id": "475ff3cc-6cbb-3c48-8aef-8f949e425cbf",
                                "text": "The most blemished life will not keep His love from pouring out. It is the blemished and the marked, the hurting and the rejected that stirs this love in Him."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
